    "# Transformer\n",
    "\n",
    "A **Transformer** is a deep learning architecture designed to process sequences (like text, audio, or time-series data) using a mechanism called **self-attention**. It was introduced in the 2017 paper:\n",
    "\n",
    "> [Attention Is All You Need](https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2017/file/3f5ee243547dee91fbd053c1c4a845aa-Paper.pdf)\n",
    "\n",
    "Transformers became the foundation of modern AI systems such as:\n",
    "\n",
    "* OpenAI’s GPT models\n",
    "* Google’s BERT\n",
    "* Image transformers in computer vision\n",
    "* Speech and translation systems\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why Transformers Were Created\n",
    "\n",
    "Before Transformers, sequence tasks mostly used:\n",
    "\n",
    "* RNNs (Recurrent Neural Networks)\n",
    "* LSTMs (Long Short-Term Memory)\n",
    "\n",
    "These models processed words **one-by-one**, which caused problems:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Problem                               | Explanation                    |\n",
    "| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n",
    "| Slow training                         | Cannot fully parallelize       |\n",
    "| Long-term memory issues               | Earlier words may be forgotten |\n",
    "| Gradient problems                     | Vanishing/exploding gradients  |\n",
    "| Hard to capture distant relationships | Context weakens over time      |\n",
    "\n",
    "Transformers solved this using:\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Attention**\n",
    "* **Parallel processing**\n",
    "* Better long-range dependency handling\n",
    "\n",
    "## Core Idea of Transformers\n",
    "\n",
    "The Transformer allows every word to look at every other word directly using:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Self-Attention\n",
    "\n",
    "> “The cat sat on the mat because it was tired.”\n",
    "\n",
    "To understand **“it”**, the model must know whether it refers to:\n",
    "\n",
    "* cat\n",
    "* mat\n",
    "\n",
    "Self-attention helps the model learn that **“it” → “cat”**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### High-Level Transformer Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "A full Transformer contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Input → Encoder → Decoder → Output\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Used in tasks like translation:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "English → Transformer → French\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Main Components\n",
    "\n",
    "The Transformer has two major parts:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Part    | Purpose           |\n",
    "| ------- | ----------------- |\n",
    "| Encoder | Understands input |\n",
    "| Decoder | Generates output  |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Encoder Structure\n",
    "\n",
    "Each encoder layer contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Multi-Head Self-Attention\n",
    "2. Feed Forward Neural Network\n",
    "3. Residual Connections\n",
    "4. Layer Normalization\n",
    "\n",
    "Usually stacked many times:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Encoder Layer × N\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Self-Attention\n",
    "\n",
    "For each word, the model computes:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Query (Q)\n",
    "* Key (K)\n",
    "* Value (V)\n",
    "\n",
    "These are learned vectors.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Intuition\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine reading a sentence:\n",
    "\n",
    "> “The animal didn’t cross the street because it was too tired.”\n",
    "\n",
    "When processing “it”, attention checks:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Which earlier words are important?\n",
    "* Which word matches context best?\n",
    "\n",
    "The model assigns scores.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Attention Formula\n",
    "\n",
    "The central formula is:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\mathrm{Attention}(Q,K,V)=\\mathrm{softmax}\\left(\\frac{QK^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}}\\right)V\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Symbol | Meaning        |\n",
    "| ------ | -------------- |\n",
    "| Q      | Query          |\n",
    "| K      | Key            |\n",
    "| V      | Value          |\n",
    "| $d_k$  | Dimension size |\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 1. Similarity Score\n",
    "\n",
    "Compute:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "QK^T\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This measures how related two words are.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 2. Scale\n",
    "\n",
    "Divide by:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\sqrt{d_k}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "This stabilizes training.\n",
    "#### 3. Softmax\n",
    "\n",
    "Convert scores into probabilities.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Word   | Attention Score |\n",
    "| ------ | --------------- |\n",
    "| animal | 0.7             |\n",
    "| street | 0.1             |\n",
    "| tired  | 0.2             |\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 4. Weighted Sum\n",
    "\n",
    "Combine values based on importance.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Positional Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "Transformers process words in parallel.\n",
    "\n",
    "But then:\n",
    "\n",
    "> How does the model know word order?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Solution:**\n",
    "\n",
    "Adds position information to embeddings.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Word | Position |\n",
    "| ---- | -------- |\n",
    "| I    | 1        |\n",
    "| love | 2        |\n",
    "| AI   | 3        |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Formula**\n",
    "\n",
    "Sinusoidal encoding:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "PE_{(pos,2i)}=\\sin\\left(\\frac{pos}{10000^{2i/d}}\\right)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "and\n",
    "$$\n",
    "PE_{(pos,2i+1)}=\\cos\\left(\\frac{pos}{10000^{2i/d}}\\right)\n",
    "$$\n"
   ]
